<title>USA: Maine would favor boycotting Midwest power plants.</title>
<headline>Maine would favor boycotting Midwest power plants.</headline>
<dateline>AUGUSTA 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Maine Gov. Angus King said he would support a boycott of Midwest power plants as part of a region-wide effort to force stricter pollution standards on other parts of the county.</p>
<p>King says much of the air pollution in Maine and other New England states comes from the Midwest, where coal-fired electric generating plants are sources of pollution.</p>
<p>Massachusetts Attorney General Scott Harshbarger has called on all Northeastern states to boycott the purchase of electric power from Midwest plants that do not meet strict anti-pollution standards.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
